        <!-- SECTION 5 -->
        <h2 id="sec-5">5. Field Tags &amp; Explicit 4-Bit Wire Types</h2>
        <p>
          Every field begins with a <strong>Tag</strong> that packs the schema field number and the
          4-bit wire type into a single Prefix-Varint:
        </p>
        <pre><code>Tag = (FieldNumber &lt;&lt; 4) | WireType</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>FieldNumber</code> is the schema field number (0 for the inline schema table, 1..N
            for message fields).
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>WireType</code> is a 4-bit unsigned integer (0..15).
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-5-1">5.1 Tag Width for Field Numbers 0..7 vs 8..1023</h3>
        <p>
          Because <code>WireType</code> occupies the low 4 bits of the tag value, the byte width of
          a tag depends only on how many bits <code>FieldNumber</code> needs:
        </p>

