        <h3 id="sec-6-1">
          6.1 <code>WireUint</code> (0) &amp; <code>WireSint</code> (12)
        </h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireUint</code> (0):
            </strong>{' '}
            Unsigned integer (<code>uint32</code>, <code>uint64</code>, <code>enum</code>) written
            as a single Prefix-Varint right after the tag.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireSint</code> (12):
            </strong>{' '}
            Signed integer (<code>int32</code>, <code>int64</code>, <code>sint32</code>,{' '}
            <code>sint64</code>) ZigZag-mapped and written as a single Prefix-Varint right after the
            tag.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">// Example 1: Field #1 (asn = 64512, WireUint = 0)</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">21</span>   <span class="text-paper font-bold">04 e0 07 00</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">64512 as 4B Prefix-Varint (LE32: 0x0007E004 &gt;&gt; 3)</span>

<span class="text-paper/75">// Example 2: Field #5 (rssi_dbm = -62, WireSint = 12)</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">b9</span>   <span class="text-paper font-bold">f7</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">-62 -&gt; ZigZag 123 -&gt; 1B Prefix-Varint (0xF7 &gt;&gt; 1 = 123)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-2">
          6.2 <code>WireBoolFalse</code> (1) &amp; <code>WireBoolTrue</code> (2)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Booleans consume <strong>0 payload bytes</strong> after the tag; the boolean value is
          carried directly in the 4-bit wire type (<code>1 = false</code>, <code>2 = true</code>).
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">65</span>   <span class="text-paper/85">// Field #3 = true  ((3 &lt;&lt; 4) | 2 = 50 -&gt; 0x65)</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">63</span>   <span class="text-paper/85">// Field #3 = false ((3 &lt;&lt; 4) | 1 = 49 -&gt; 0x63)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-3">
          6.3 <code>WireString</code> (3) &amp; <code>WireBytes</code> (4)
        </h3>
        <p>
          The tag is followed by <code>[ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)]</code> and{' '}
          <code>[ByteLen raw bytes]</code>. Strings are UTF-8 encoded without a NUL terminator.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">47</span>   <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">09</span>     <span class="text-paper font-bold">72 74 72 31</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span>  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">Len=4</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">"rtr1" (Field #2, 4 UTF-8 bytes)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-4">
          6.4 <code>WireSubMsg</code> (5)
        </h3>
        <p>
          <code>WireSubMsg</code> encodes a nested message as{' '}
          <code>[ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)][Inner Message Bytes]</code>. Single-pass encoders reserve
          a 2-byte Prefix-Varint slot (<code>TZCNT = 1</code>) for <code>ByteLen</code> and patch it
          after writing the nested fields; decoders accept any valid Prefix-Varint width.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">// Inner Location message (city = "FRA" at #3, rack = 42 at #4):</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">67</span> <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">07</span> <span class="text-paper">46 52 41</span>   <span class="text-paper/75">// #3: "FRA" (5 bytes)</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">81</span> <span class="text-paper">55</span>            <span class="text-paper/75">// #4: 42    (2 bytes)</span>

<span class="text-paper/75">// Outer Field #9 wrapping the 7-byte inner message:</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">56 02</span>  <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">1e 00</span>  <span class="text-paper font-bold">67 07 46 52 41 81 55</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag#9</span>  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">Len=7</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">Inner Sub-Message (7 bytes)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-5">
          6.5 <code>WireStringArr</code> (6)
        </h3>
        <p>
          <code>WireStringArr</code> encodes <code>repeated string</code> or{' '}
          <code>repeated bytes</code> with an outer <code>ByteLen</code> prefix followed by{' '}
          <code>ElemCount</code> and each length-prefixed element, so a reader can skip the entire
          list in one addition (<code>pos += ByteLen</code>):
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">Layout:  [Tag] [ByteLen] [ElemCount] [StrLen_0][Bytes_0] ... [StrLen_N-1][Bytes_N-1]</span>

<span class="text-paper/75">// Example: Field #7 (tags = ["a", "bc"])</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">ed</span>   <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">1a 00</span>  <span class="text-acid">05</span>   <span class="text-paper">03 61</span>   <span class="text-paper">05 62 63</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span>  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">Len=6</span>  <span class="text-acid">N=2</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">"a"     "bc"</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-6">
          6.6 <code>WireUintArr</code> (7) &amp; <code>WireSintArr</code> (13)
        </h3>
        <p>
          These wire types encode a packed array of unsigned (<code>WireUintArr</code>) or
          ZigZag-signed (<code>WireSintArr</code>) varints with an outer <code>ByteLen</code> prefix
          and <code>ElemCount</code>:
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">Layout:  [Tag] [ByteLen] [ElemCount] [Elem_0] ... [Elem_N-1]</span>

<span class="text-paper/75">// Example: Field #8 (prefixes = [10, 300])</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">1e 02</span>  <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">12 00</span>  <span class="text-acid">05</span>   <span class="text-paper">15</span>  <span class="text-paper">b2 04</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag#8</span>  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">Len=4</span>  <span class="text-acid">N=2</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">10  300</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-7">
          6.7 <code>WireSubMsgArr</code> (8)
        </h3>
        <p>
          <code>WireSubMsgArr</code> encodes <code>repeated message</code> inside a single outer{' '}
          <code>ByteLen</code> container followed by length-prefixed sub-message elements:
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">Layout:  [Tag] [ByteLen] [ElemLen_0][Elem_0] ... [ElemLen_N-1][Elem_N-1]</span>
<span class="text-paper/75">                         |&lt;-------------- ByteLen bytes --------------&gt;|</span></code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Each element <code>i</code> starts with its byte length <code>ElemLen_i</code>{' '}
            (Prefix-Varint) followed by <code>ElemLen_i</code> bytes of the element message.
          </li>
          <li>
            The sum of all <code>len(ElemLen_i) + ElemLen_i</code> across elements MUST equal{' '}
            <code>ByteLen</code>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-6-8">
          6.8 <code>WireMap</code> (9)
        </h3>
        <p>
          <code>WireMap</code> encodes <code>map&lt;K, V&gt;</code> directly inside one
          length-prefixed container without synthetic <code>MapEntry</code> wrapper sub-messages:
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">Layout:  [Tag] [ByteLen] [MapType (1B)] [EntryCount] [Key_0][Val_0] ...</span>
<span class="text-paper/75">                         |&lt;-------------- ByteLen bytes -------------&gt;|</span></code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              1-Byte <code>MapType</code> Header:
            </strong>{' '}
            Encodes <code>(KeyWireType &lt;&lt; 4) | ValWireType</code>:
            <ul>
              <li>
                <code>KeyWireType</code>: <code>WireUint</code> (0), <code>WireString</code> (3),{' '}
                <code>WireFixed32</code> (10), <code>WireFixed64</code> (11), or{' '}
                <code>WireSint</code> (12).
              </li>
              <li>
                <code>ValWireType</code>: <code>WireUint</code> (0), <code>WireString</code> (3),{' '}
                <code>WireBytes</code> (4), <code>WireSubMsg</code> (5), <code>WireFixed32</code>{' '}
                (10), <code>WireFixed64</code> (11), or <code>WireSint</code> (12).
              </li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Minimum Container Length:</strong> Because every <code>WireMap</code> includes
            the 1-byte <code>MapType</code> and at least 1 byte for <code>EntryCount</code>,{' '}
            <code>ByteLen</code> MUST be at least 2.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Untagged Entries &amp; Unordered Keys:</strong> Each entry writes the raw
            payload of <code>KeyWireType</code> followed by the raw payload of{' '}
            <code>ValWireType</code>. Keys may appear in any order; duplicate keys follow "last
            write wins".
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-6-9">
          6.9 <code>WireFixed32</code> (10) &amp; <code>WireFixed64</code> (11)
        </h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireFixed32</code> (10):
            </strong>{' '}
            4 bytes in little-endian order (<code>float</code>, <code>fixed32</code>,{' '}
            <code>sfixed32</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireFixed64</code> (11):
            </strong>{' '}
            8 bytes in little-endian order (<code>double</code>, <code>fixed64</code>,{' '}
            <code>sfixed64</code>).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">// Example: Field #6 (cpu_load = 0.5 as float64)</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">d7</span>   <span class="text-paper font-bold">00 00 00 00 00 00 e0 3f</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">IEEE-754 0.5 (8 bytes little-endian)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-10">
          6.10 <code>WireFixedArr</code> (14)
        </h3>
        <p>
          <code>WireFixedArr</code> encodes a packed array of fixed-width 32-bit or 64-bit
          little-endian elements with an outer <code>ByteLen</code> prefix and a 1-byte{' '}
          <code>ElemType</code> header:
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">Layout:  [Tag] [ByteLen] [ElemType (1B: 10 or 11)] [Little-Endian Elements...]</span>
<span class="text-paper/75">                         |&lt;------------------ ByteLen bytes -----------------&gt;|</span></code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>ElemType = 10</code> (<code>WireFixed32</code>): The header is followed by{' '}
            <code>(ByteLen - 1) / 4</code> 4-byte elements.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>ElemType = 11</code> (<code>WireFixed64</code>): The header is followed by{' '}
            <code>(ByteLen - 1) / 8</code> 8-byte elements.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-6-11">
          6.11 <code>WireExtended</code> (15)
        </h3>
        <p>
          <code>WireExtended</code> reserves wire type 15 as a length-prefixed extension escape
          hatch capable of expressing up to 256 extended wire types while remaining skippable in{' '}
          <code>O(1)</code> time:
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/75">Layout:  [Tag] [ByteLen] [ExtType (1B: 0..255)] [ExtPayload (ByteLen - 1 bytes)]</span>
<span class="text-paper/75">                         |&lt;------------------- ByteLen bytes -----------------&gt;|</span></code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Because <code>WireExtended</code> starts with <code>ByteLen</code> just like every other
            container, existing decoders can skip unknown extended fields in a single jump (
            <code>pos += ByteLen</code>).
          </li>
        </ul>

        <!-- SECTION 7 -->
        <h2 id="sec-7">
          7. Branchless <code>TZCNT</code> Header-Hop Field Lookup (<code>LocateField</code>)
        </h2>
        <p>
          In Protocol Buffers, skipping a preceding varint field requires a byte-by-byte loop. In
          OmniBuf, every scalar width is known from <code>b[0]</code>, booleans are 0 value bytes,
          and every container starts with <code>ByteLen</code>, so <code>LocateField</code> jumps
          across fields in <code>O(1)</code> time per field:
        </p>
        <div class="my-4 p-4 bg-ink text-paper border-2 border-ink rounded-md font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed [&>pre]:!bg-transparent [&>pre]:!p-0 [&>pre]:!m-0 [&>pre]:!border-0">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2.5 pb-2 border-b border-paper/15">
            <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-acid">O(1) Header-Hop Field Lookup</div>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-copy={locateFieldGoCode}
              class="copy-snippet-btn min-w-[4.75rem] text-center px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase bg-paper/15 hover:bg-acid hover:text-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-acid text-paper border border-paper/30 rounded shrink-0 transition"
            >
              Copy
            </button>
          </div>
          <Code code={locateFieldGoCode} lang="go" theme="github-dark" />
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 8 -->
        <h2 id="sec-8">
          8. Optional Inline Schema (<code>Field #0</code>, <code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code>)
        </h2>
        <p>
          When self-describing mode is enabled, <strong>Field #0</strong> (<code>Tag = 0x0B</code>,{' '}
          <code>WireSubMsg = 5</code>) is written at byte 0 of the message as a standard OmniBuf
          sub-message encoding <code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code>.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Zero-Cost Skipping for Schema-Aware Decoders:</strong> Because Field #0 is a
            normal <code>WireSubMsg</code> starting with <code>ByteLen</code>, schema-aware decoders
            read <code>ByteLen</code> and jump over the entire metadata block in one addition.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Extensible via <code>.proto</code>:
            </strong>{' '}
            Because <code>SchemaMeta</code> is a normal Protobuf message (
            <code>proto/omnibuf/v1/meta.proto</code>), future optional metadata fields can be
            added without changing the wire format.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-8-1">
          8.1 <code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code> Definition (<code>meta.proto</code>)
        </h3>
        <div class="my-4 p-4 bg-ink text-paper border-2 border-ink rounded-md font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed [&>pre]:!bg-transparent [&>pre]:!p-0 [&>pre]:!m-0 [&>pre]:!border-0">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2.5 pb-2 border-b border-paper/15">
            <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-acid">proto/omnibuf/v1/meta.proto</div>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-copy={sec8MetaProtoCode}
              class="copy-snippet-btn min-w-[4.75rem] text-center px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase bg-paper/15 hover:bg-acid hover:text-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-acid text-paper border border-paper/30 rounded shrink-0 transition"
            >
              Copy
            </button>
          </div>
          <Code code={sec8MetaProtoCode} lang="protobuf" theme="github-dark" />
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Keyed by FieldNumber (<code>fields = 2</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Maps each field number to its name (<code>1 &rarr; "id"</code>), so omitted optional
            fields never shift field names.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Hoisted Child Schemas (<code>children = 3</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Maps a parent field number (for a nested sub-message, sub-message array, or map value)
            to its child <code>SchemaMeta</code> so repeated sub-messages only encode their field
            names once.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-8-2">
          8.2 Single Message Wire Encoding with <code>Field #0</code>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Consider a <code>Location</code> message (<code>city = "FRA"</code> at #3,{' '}
          <code>rack = 42</code> at #4) encoded with <code>Field #0</code> (
          <code>type_name = "Location"</code>,{' '}
          <code>fields = &#123;3: "city", 4: "rack"&#125;</code>):
        </p>

        <!-- Responsive Annotated Byte Breakdown (No Cramped Mobile Columns) -->
        <div class="my-4 border-2 border-ink rounded-md bg-white overflow-hidden">
